set - shows the system path to your command line
ver - shows OS version you're on
systeminfo - show's more indepth info about the system
    pipe through more to show page by page
help provides more info for the specified command
cls clears the command prompt screen

ping
ipconfig and ipconfig /all
tracert
netstat - displays current network connections
    and listening ports
        -a displays all established connections
        -b shows associated program
        -o reveals PID associated with each connection
        -n numerical form for addresses and port #s

cd and dir
dir /a - displays hidden and system files as well
dir /s displays files in current tree recursively

tree visually represents the tree

type - view text files
    useful to pipe through more for longer files

tasklist - task manager equivalent for cmd line
    taskkill /PID <PID#>
